# The node detail as a column of cards.
#
# The screen this replaced was a hundred and twenty label-and-value rows with dimmed words
# between them, which is a group distinguished from its own rows by colour alone. What a card
# says instead is said by a fill and an edge, and there are three things about doing that in a
# *scrolling* list that a still of the top of the screen cannot show. So this walks down.
#
# Row 0 of the Nodes list is the Map, so a node's row is its index in the demo roster plus one -
# Echo Repeater is seeds[5] and row 6. It is the node worth opening here because it reports
# nearly everything: actions, identity, signal, an environment reading with a bar under it, a
# two-channel power monitor and both neighbour groups, which is six cards and a cut one.

scene demo
tab nodes
key down 6
key a
hold 1200

# The cursor on the first verb's switch, which is the one control that lays a ground of its own.
# It has to lay the *card's* rather than the panel's, or it punches a black hole in the card on
# precisely the row being pointed at.
key down 1
hold 1200

# Down through the groups. What to watch is the card the window is cutting: it keeps square
# corners and its full width on the cut end, because a rounded corner halfway down a scroll is a
# card claiming to end where the panel merely stopped.
key down 8
hold 800
key down 8
hold 800
key down 8
hold 1600

# And back up, so the cut lands on the other end of a card as well.
key up 12
hold 1600
